    <briefdescription>
<para>Accumulates per-run fault counters by listening to a <ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_listening_scraper_diagnostic_sink" kindref="compound">ListeningScraperDiagnosticSink</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Attach once before the run starts via <ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_scraper_run_summary_collector_1a2e5c5db25c789f35367c04790867e005" kindref="member">attach()</ref>. After the run completes, call <ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_scraper_run_summary_collector_1a975bf589e3dbeefde0eae7b930bae407" kindref="member">recordSuccess()</ref> and <ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_scraper_run_summary_collector_1a6276fee46324ad58a325d9f1e1d82150" kindref="member">setRunStats()</ref>, then retrieve the snapshot with <ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_scraper_run_summary_collector_1afb1308c3b9ab678df014d891c9d8b5b8" kindref="member">summary()</ref>.</para>
<para>Thread-safety: all public methods are thread-safe; the listener lambda installed by <ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_scraper_run_summary_collector_1a2e5c5db25c789f35367c04790867e005" kindref="member">attach()</ref> may be invoked concurrently from the scraper bounded thread pool. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
